  "caption": "The von Neumann stability limit dt = 0.04651 ms is the limit the code obeys, and it fails in the predicted way: the growing component is the checkerboard mode k = pi/dx, not generic noise. Measured amplification matches the closed-form |1 - 4D dt/dx^2| to 2.2e-16. Failure is first seen at 1.065 times the limit rather than exactly at it, because |f_V| = 3 is an upper bound taken at the excited root V3 = 1.986 whereas the solution peaks at only 1.691; using that peak predicts 1.027. Ignoring the reaction term entirely would give 0.0500 ms, 7.5 % too optimistic.",
